    "explicit_requirements": [
      "Produce a variance analysis Excel workbook comparing UNH's Q1 2026 CostOfGoodsAndServicesSold ($12.823B) and SellingGeneralAndAdministrativeExpense ($15.39B) against prior-quarter and prior-year benchmarks to quantify cost overruns as a percentage of Revenues ($111.721B).",
      "Calculate and present gross margin variance (Revenues minus CostOfGoodsAndServicesSold) and operating margin variance (OperatingIncomeLoss divided by Revenues) with clear bridge from prior period to current period.",
      "Isolate the impact of cost overruns on OperatingIncomeLoss ($8.99B) by decomposing variance into volume, price, and mix components where data permits.",
      "Flag any line items where the cost overrun exceeds 200 basis points relative to the trailing four-quarter average, and label these as material deviations.",
      "Include a summary dashboard tab with key metrics: revenue growth rate, cost-to-revenue ratio change, and diluted EPS variance ($6.9/share) linked to cost drivers.",
      "Structure the workbook with separate tabs for raw data inputs, variance calculations, and executive summary, with all assumptions documented in a dedicated notes tab.",
      "Cross-reference findings against UNH's historical SEC EDGAR filings (CIK 0000731766) to validate trend consistency and identify any one-time items distorting the variance.",
      "Deliver the final workbook by 2026-05-22 end-of-day, formatted for direct inclusion in a client pitchbook without further rework."
    ],
    "implicit_requirements": [
      "Use standard investment banking variance analysis format: waterfall charts or bridge tables showing incremental contribution of each cost component to total overrun.",
      "All monetary figures must be in USD millions with one decimal place, consistent with UNH's filing conventions.",
      "Apply healthcare insurance sector-specific cost classifications (e.g., medical loss ratio components) where UNH's segment disclosures permit disaggregation.",
      "Maintain full audit trail: every calculated cell must trace back to a pinned fact or a clearly labeled assumption.",
      "Use color coding (red/green) to highlight positive/negative variances per banking presentation standards.",
      "Embed formulas rather than hardcoded values where possible to allow scenario sensitivity testing.",
      "Include a peer comparison stub tab referencing sector benchmarks for cost-to-revenue ratios in healthcare insurance, even if populated with placeholder structure."
    ],
